I acquired an InkShield from this [http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/1908026860/inkshield-an-open-source-inkjet-shield-for-arduino Kickstarter]. My goal for this project is to have a smallish enclosure to contain the system and buttons on the top which allow different messages to be printed.
<img src="https://www.bloominglabs.org/Special:FilePath/Inkshield001b.jpg" alt="InkShield PCB">

== Build ==
So this worked out pretty nice, the code reads 5 button values from the free analog input 5. Just holding the button down repeats the messages printed. You can see that different font widths can be achieved by moving the print head faster or slower.

